1
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:48,979
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:51,870
[Episode 25]

3
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:03,790
Lin Zhixia?

4
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:06,840
Lin Zhixia?

5
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,590
Lin Zhixia.

6
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:26,400
♪ The narcissus rides the carp,
fading away in decay ♪

7
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:33,880
♪ Dark‑green lurks beneath the sea,
stirring the nebulae ♪

8
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:41,440
♪ Through countless nights,
you and I march onward ♪

9
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:48,579
♪ Probing, waking, and gathering
love gone mad ♪

10
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:54,860
♪ Say yes, and let the present reset ♪

11
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:59,130
♪ Our first night, my sunset ♪

12
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:02,810
♪ The whole world, just us two ♪

13
00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:06,370
♪ Sleepless city, rising and falling ♪

14
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:10,480
♪ Breathing the faint hush of midnight ♪

15
00:04:11,050 --> 00:04:13,540
♪ All around, someone strikes the fire ♪

16
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,280
♪ Lovers burn and wound one another ♪

17
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:41,720
[Electrocardiogram Report]

18
00:04:41,830 --> 00:04:44,360
[Electroencephalogram Report]

19
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,159
I just feel a bit flustered

20
00:04:46,510 --> 00:04:47,710
and can't sleep well.

21
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,450
Sometimes I feel my heart
beating really fast,

22
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,510
and...

23
00:04:53,070 --> 00:04:55,000
I feel hot for no reason.

24
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,760
According to the report,

25
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,630
your blood indicators,

26
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:02,510
ECG, and EEG are all fine.

27
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:07,990
Are you under too much pressure
at work lately?

28
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,480
Not really.

29
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:15,470
Well then,

30
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,310
you can do a Holter monitor test first.

31
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:19,120
You have to wear this for 24 hours,

32
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,250
even when you sleep.

33
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,260
Then we'll see how it goes.

34
00:05:22,270 --> 00:05:23,210
If that doesn't work,

35
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:25,470
we'll do a CT scan
of your heart and brain.

36
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,750
Is that necessary? It's so much trouble.

37
00:05:27,750 --> 00:05:29,410
You have to take it seriously.

38
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:39,510
Your sleep quality really isn't great.

39
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:40,909
It's not serious, right?

40
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:42,330
It's not a big problem.

41
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,000
At around 7:30 last night,

42
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,170
what were you doing?

43
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:51,170
Your heart rate was a bit fast.

44
00:05:51,830 --> 00:05:52,630
7:30?

45
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:53,720
Yes.

46
00:05:55,150 --> 00:05:56,720
7:30...

47
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:01,960
Jiang Yubai chatted with me
for a bit after dinner.

48
00:06:08,510 --> 00:06:09,160
Alright.

49
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:11,390
I know the reason now.

50
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,870
What is it?

51
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,650
It's just the changing of seasons.

52
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,210
Plus you're a bit nervous.

53
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,040
Just rest more

54
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:26,430
and don't overthink.

55
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,120
But I can't sleep.

56
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,450
Can you prescribe me some sleeping pills?

57
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:34,600
You can't take sleeping pills
for no good reason.

58
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,240
I'm reviewing your report out of goodwill.

59
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,510
You're not even
a patient of my department.

60
00:06:37,510 --> 00:06:38,630
How can I prescribe them for you?

61
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:40,600
Are you sure I have no problems?

62
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:42,000
I'm sure.

63
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:48,630
Now off you go.

64
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,150
I need to do my rounds.

65
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,770
Shen Fuxuan insisted I'm not sick.

66
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:57,240
But I really feel unwell lately.

67
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:58,560
However, the checkup results

68
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,220
do show that nothing is wrong.

69
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,680
What do those straight guys know?

70
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,540
Tell me, where do you feel unwell?

71
00:07:08,790 --> 00:07:10,450
When I interact with someone,

72
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,600
I get nervous for no reason.

73
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:15,210
I can't sleep well either.

74
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,240
Sometimes my heart beats so fast

75
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:19,570
that it feels like it's going to jump out.

76
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,000
Interact with someone?

77
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:24,570
Who? Jiang Yubai?

78
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,120
How do you know?

79
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:31,330
I think Shen Fuxuan is right.

80
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:33,370
You are not sick.

81
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:35,560
It's a kind of stress response.

82
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,580
A stress response?

83
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,560
It's like a problem

84
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,120
we often encounter during puberty.

85
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,430
We've had it before.

86
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,240
But everyone is different.

87
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,600
In puberty, there are early
and late bloomers,

88
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,940
just like in menopause.

89
00:07:48,159 --> 00:07:50,560
Basically, your puberty is here now.

90
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:54,680
Then what should I do?

91
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,040
I have a folk prescription.

92
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,000
What is it?

93
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:02,240
A desensitization therapy.
We'll fight poison with poison.

94
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,360
Aren't you afraid of him getting close?

95
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,800
Then you should get close to him first.

96
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,870
Hug him, cuddle him, and hold his hand.

97
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,430
After enough exposure and attempts,

98
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:11,960
your body will naturally
become immune to it.

99
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:15,240
Will it work?

100
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,450
What's the principle behind it?

101
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:18,750
Don't ask.

102
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,680
Just try it.

103
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:41,870
Lin Zhixia.

104
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:46,080
Why do you suddenly want to play
a horror escape room?

105
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:50,510
I had some problems with my research.

106
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:52,170
So I came to find some answers.

107
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,480
You can find answers here?

108
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,730
I can look at the mechanisms and stuff.

109
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,600
My bad, my bad.

110
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:49,330
I forgot to consider
personal tolerance levels.

111
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,600
Should we continue
the desensitization then?

112
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,390
Of course.

113
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,850
If your experiment fails once,

114
00:09:53,850 --> 00:09:54,840
would you just stop?

115
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,840
Besides, you did great this time.

116
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,900
We'll definitely succeed next time.

117
00:09:59,030 --> 00:10:00,030
What's next then?

118
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,720
The cinema.

119
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,040
It's a bit hot in here.

120
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,360
Let's go out.

121
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,250
This movie isn't very good anyway.

122
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:50,030
Let's go.

123
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,770
I'm speechless.

124
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:57,600
I really am.

125
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,080
The way your brain is wired

126
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,740
is definitely different
from ordinary people.

127
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:04,840
Even a rock would get it by now.

128
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:10,750
What's wrong?

129
00:12:11,270 --> 00:12:11,800
Nothing.

130
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:13,680
It's my problem.

131
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,630
My fault.

132
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:16,820
Don't blame yourself.

133
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,200
I really don't
quite understand this problem.

134
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,360
But if, like you said,

135
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,840
everyone goes through it,

136
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,490
then I'll accept it.

137
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,840
I can overcome it too.

138
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,840
You can do it.

139
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,850
Take your time to figure it out.

140
00:12:45,030 --> 00:12:48,360
We asked you to come home
these past few days, but you didn't.

141
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,440
Your mother and I still want to have

142
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,570
a good talk with you.

143
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:56,840
Go ahead.

144
00:12:58,030 --> 00:12:59,360
About you and Lin Zeqiu,

145
00:13:01,150 --> 00:13:02,410
we don't approve of it.

146
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,010
Didn't you want me to date someone?

147
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,360
Lin Zeqiu is a good person

148
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,270
with a good job.

149
00:13:11,270 --> 00:13:13,840
He got into a big tech company right after
graduation, and his salary is good too.

150
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,600
We've known each other since
childhood and know each other inside out.

151
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,330
What's there to disapprove of?

152
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,370
With your qualifications,

153
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:21,670
you could even find someone
better than Li Zhe.

154
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:22,910
Why Lin Zeqiu?

155
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:23,960
I don't get it.

156
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,960
I like him.

157
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,440
You like him?

158
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:31,670
In the grand scheme of your life,

159
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:34,960
liking something or not
is the least important consideration.

160
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:35,750
Baihui.

161
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:39,050
We really are doing this
for your own good.

162
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,640
When you were little,
we made you study hard

163
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,000
and not waste time and energy

164
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,440
on other things.

165
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:47,920
It was all so you could
get into Qingbei University

166
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:49,670
and lay a good foundation for your life.

167
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:50,790
You did it.

168
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,030
You stood on a starting line

169
00:13:52,030 --> 00:13:53,870
that's different from others.

170
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,690
This proves that we were right.

171
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:57,550
Now,

172
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,080
we want you to find a better partner

173
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,550
so that your future life

174
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:02,880
will be free of worries.

175
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,120
Your dad and I

176
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:09,090
are pretty much set
in our ways for this life.

177
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,600
I don't want you to spend
the rest of your life

178
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,750
living like us,

179
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:13,600
feeling stifled.

180
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:17,030
But I don't think you two
are living a stifled life.

181
00:14:17,030 --> 00:14:18,030
And I'm confident that,

182
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:19,380
with Lin Zeqiu's and my abilities,

183
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,600
we can live a good life
together in the future.

184
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,960
He works himself to the bone,
but he's just an employee.

185
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,510
He can make some money when he's young,

186
00:14:25,510 --> 00:14:27,480
but his family background isn't strong
enough to weather any storms.

187
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,870
In the future, you'll have kids,
a mortgage, and car loans.

188
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:32,080
You'll face a lot of pressure
when you're middle-aged.

189
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,840
You don't see these problems now,

190
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,360
but that doesn't mean they won't appear.

191
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:36,510
How can we not worry?

192
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,960
But Li Zhe's family wouldn't
have this problem.

193
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:41,240
Even if your family encounters problems,

194
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,750
Li Zhe's family members are all local

195
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,080
and can provide a lot of help.

196
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,840
Tell me, you could have a life
with a house, a car,

197
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,630
and a nanny, but you choose not to.

198
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:49,120
What's the point of working
so hard every day?

199
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,120
But I don't care about those things.

200
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,150
I don't need a big house.

201
00:14:53,150 --> 00:14:54,510
I don't need a nanny.

202
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:57,150
I just want to live a simple life

203
00:14:57,150 --> 00:14:58,600
with the person I like in the future.

204
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:01,400
Jin Baihui, do you not understand
what I'm saying?

205
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,030
Your mother and I won't need you
to take care of us in the future.

206
00:15:05,030 --> 00:15:05,960
But don't you know

207
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,030
the family situation

208
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:07,720
of that Lin guy?

209
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,050
Can he just ignore them?

210
00:15:09,390 --> 00:15:10,870
You worked so hard to get into
Qingbei University,

211
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:12,600
just to find a family like this?

212
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,120
Baihui.

213
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:17,200
We really are doing this
for your own good.

214
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:19,840
I'm telling you, this is not a discussion.

215
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,770
Move back home immediately today.

216
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:24,750
We agreed to talk nicely.

217
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:25,390
Look at her.

218
00:15:25,390 --> 00:15:27,590
She won't listen to anything right now.

219
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,000
Baihui.

220
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,390
You really need to listen.

221
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:32,920
I've listened long enough.

222
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,630
Please stop doing things for my own good.

223
00:15:38,750 --> 00:15:39,750
I'm not moving.

224
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,510
I'll decide this for myself.

225
00:15:56,670 --> 00:15:57,170
Ms. Zhou.

226
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:59,270
These are the new business collaborations
for Su Mo this week.

227
00:15:59,270 --> 00:16:02,330
It seems his new drama has
brought him high popularity.

228
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,750
Even though there are no major brands,

229
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:07,510
the brand tone is quite good.

230
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:09,910
The positioning is quite smart.

231
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:10,840
Interesting.

232
00:16:14,030 --> 00:16:16,390
Su Mo, why are you at the company?

233
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:18,920
Ms. Zhou, I came to deliver a contract.

234
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,600
Your momentum is pretty good lately.

235
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,790
Even though those
external collaborations are small,

236
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,590
you are making steady progress.

237
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:26,800
Thank you, Ms. Zhou.

238
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:29,320
It's all thanks to Tingting.

239
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,960
The company's resources are limited.

240
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,510
Sometimes,

241
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:38,730
following the right person is more
important than doing the right thing.

242
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:39,750
You're smart.

243
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,410
You should understand what I mean.

244
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,320
Su Mo.

245
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:47,390
Tingting.

246
00:16:49,390 --> 00:16:50,080
What's wrong, Ms. Zhou?

247
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:52,140
Is there a problem with the contract?

248
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,940
It's nothing. I was praising you.

249
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:57,390
This newbie of yours has good taste.

250
00:17:03,150 --> 00:17:03,950
What's wrong?

251
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,920
Did Ms. Zhou make things
difficult for you?

252
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:05,680
No.

253
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,750
I was just passing by.
So I had a chat with her.

254
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:08,510
About what?

255
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:10,960
Nothing.

256
00:17:11,589 --> 00:17:12,880
Just a casual chat.

257
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:14,270
Don't worry.

258
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:16,720
I'll go deliver a contract first.

259
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:28,940
[Star Shine Media]

260
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:46,520
[Duan Qiyan]

261
00:17:48,870 --> 00:17:49,350
[Duan Qiyan]

262
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,170
[What are you doing?]

263
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:01,260
[Same place tonight.]

264
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,170
[Hey, reply if you see this.]

265
00:18:05,210 --> 00:18:07,380
[Hey!]

266
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,170
[Are you going or not?]

267
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:12,940
[Are you there, Tang Tingting?]

268
00:18:11,790 --> 00:18:13,250
I'm busy. Don't bother me.

269
00:18:17,750 --> 00:18:18,910
[What are you doing?]

270
00:18:19,050 --> 00:18:19,920
[Are you there, Tang Tingting?]

271
00:18:19,950 --> 00:18:20,930
[What's wrong?]

272
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:21,870
[Are you angry?]

273
00:18:21,890 --> 00:18:22,680
[I'll treat you to dinner. Don't be mad.]

274
00:18:43,070 --> 00:18:43,790
Zhixia,

275
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,550
why the sudden call?

276
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:48,880
There's something I might need to
trouble you with.

277
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,030
It's no trouble. Just tell me.

278
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,000
I'll send you a paper in a bit.

279
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,680
Professor Lin,

280
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,440
I'm just a university undergraduate.

281
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,270
Would I even understand
the paper you send?

282
00:18:59,270 --> 00:19:01,270
Did Tang Tingting ask you to mock me?

283
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:02,400
Of course not.

284
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,790
I want to apply for the
national project next month.

285
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:06,920
That's a good thing.

286
00:19:07,030 --> 00:19:08,400
You can definitely do it.

287
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,200
But to apply,

288
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:12,030
I need recommendations from at least
2 doctoral supervisors in the field.

289
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:14,480
The professors in our school
with relevant expertise

290
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:16,830
have their recommendation spots
booked long ago.

291
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:18,290
So I wanted to ask you about

292
00:19:18,310 --> 00:19:21,750
Professor Liu Qingsong in your
university's School of Mathematics,

293
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:23,270
the one who does
partial differential equations

294
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:25,000
and computational mathematics.

295
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,460
He's a leading figure
in our domestic field.

296
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,830
I wanted to ask if you know him.

297
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,680
Could you put in a good word for me

298
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,790
or introduce me?

299
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,670
I just want a chance

300
00:19:36,030 --> 00:19:37,760
to show him our group's report.

301
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:39,280
I understand.

302
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:40,790
Prof Liu

303
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:42,850
is indeed the treasure of our school.

304
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,590
He supervised my major advisor back then,

305
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:47,240
so in terms of seniority,

306
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,040
he's actually my grand-master.

307
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:51,070
I can ask my advisor for you,

308
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,400
and let him give it a try.

309
00:19:52,510 --> 00:19:54,440
But Prof Liu is very stubborn,

310
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,640
so I can't guarantee it will work.

311
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,890
It's fine. Don't feel pressured.

312
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:00,490
I'm just hoping for a chance

313
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,960
for him to see our project.

314
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,480
The project will speak for itself.

315
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:04,160
Okay.

316
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,480
How about this?

317
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,350
Tonight,

318
00:20:06,350 --> 00:20:08,510
I'll ask my teacher to try.

319
00:20:08,510 --> 00:20:10,070
I'll feel him out first.

320
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:11,790
Thank you, Duan.

321
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,170
Don't mention it. Wait for my news.

322
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,550
It crashed again?

323
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:50,120
[Cancel] [Post]

324
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,890
The computer died before I did.

325
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:48,720
My stomach is protesting.

326
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:50,200
My brain has gone on strike.

327
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,720
Help me.

328
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:17,160
Su Mo?

329
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,590
I saw on your Moments

330
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:21,210
that your computer broke.

331
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:22,970
I happened to be nearby.

332
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:25,840
So I bought some
late-night snacks for you.

333
00:21:27,310 --> 00:21:28,000
Come on.

334
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:29,590
Eat over here.

335
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:31,160
Let me take a look at your computer.

336
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,000
Can you do it?

337
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,920
I'll try.

338
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,790
Gamers are all computer experts.

339
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,700
Alright, give it a try.

340
00:21:50,770 --> 00:21:59,420
[Tang Tingting]

341
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:58,880
Being handsome is just one of
my Su Mo's many strengths.

342
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,510
Handsome?

343
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,500
How handsome can he be?

344
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:22,480
Tingting.

345
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:25,030
Ms. Zhou came to me today

346
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:28,350
because she wanted me to join her team.

347
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,440
I turned her down.

348
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,200
I know I made it to where I am today

349
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,590
because when I was at my lowest,

350
00:22:42,590 --> 00:22:43,920
you didn't give up on me.

351
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:47,550
I know how much pressure
you've shouldered for me.

352
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:52,960
I didn't tell you then

353
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:55,270
because I was afraid of upsetting you

354
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,470
and making you think I didn't trust you.

355
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,720
I'm telling you now

356
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:03,310
because I think the credit
for fixing the computer

357
00:23:03,310 --> 00:23:05,960
should make up
for me keeping things from you.

358
00:23:14,590 --> 00:23:15,400
Tingting.

359
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:17,830
It's fixed.

360
00:23:32,270 --> 00:23:33,160
Brat,

361
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:35,370
at least you have a conscience.

362
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:07,620
[School of Mathematical Sciences
Experimental Center, Qingbei University]

363
00:24:15,210 --> 00:24:19,020
[School of Mathematical Sciences
Experimental Center, Qingbei University]

364
00:24:25,550 --> 00:24:26,400
Engineer Xie,

365
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:28,350
please temporarily reduce
the resource quota for my project

366
00:24:28,350 --> 00:24:30,000
by a quarter,

367
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:32,600
and give it to Dr. Lin's group.

368
00:24:34,330 --> 00:24:35,050
Dr. Tan,

369
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:36,460
didn't you say before...

370
00:24:36,460 --> 00:24:37,340
I know.

371
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:39,510
Just do as I said.

372
00:24:39,550 --> 00:24:41,750
You can inform their group
about the new schedule.

373
00:24:41,750 --> 00:24:42,400
Thank you.

374
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,340
Why are you here for no reason?

375
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:11,640
How harsh of you.

376
00:25:12,110 --> 00:25:14,240
Can't I hang out with you for no reason?

377
00:25:26,590 --> 00:25:28,550
Tang, calm down.

378
00:25:29,310 --> 00:25:31,110
First, tell me why you're angry.

379
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:35,280
And where did this
inverse function come from?

380
00:25:47,790 --> 00:25:48,590
Jiang,

381
00:25:49,310 --> 00:25:50,400
I really don't understand

382
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:52,510
how I provoked Tang Tingting.

383
00:25:52,530 --> 00:25:54,590
She hasn't talked to me for days.

384
00:25:54,750 --> 00:25:56,400
I sent her so many messages,

385
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:59,730
and she only replied with a smile emoji.
What does that mean?

386
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,400
You're upset over that?

387
00:26:04,790 --> 00:26:06,400
Don't you know her?

388
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:08,350
She's been violent since childhood.

389
00:26:08,350 --> 00:26:10,280
I could handle physical violence,

390
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:12,160
but now she's learned
the silent treatment.

391
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:14,440
Isn't that more hurtful?

392
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:16,110
I'd rather she punched me.

393
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:19,880
Then I can only wish you strength.

394
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:24,590
What's wrong with girls?

395
00:26:24,590 --> 00:26:26,510
They weren't like this in school.

396
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:28,200
Why is it that the older they get

397
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:31,600
and the longer we spend together,
the less I understand them?

398
00:26:44,550 --> 00:26:45,350
Mr. Tao.

399
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:47,510
Qiyan.

400
00:26:48,850 --> 00:26:50,660
About asking Professor Liu

401
00:26:50,660 --> 00:26:52,920
to recommend the project
you mentioned earlier...

402
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:53,960
Yes, Mr. Tao.

403
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:54,750
How did it go?

404
00:26:55,750 --> 00:26:56,510
This afternoon,

405
00:26:56,510 --> 00:26:58,240
I went specifically to see him.

406
00:26:58,440 --> 00:27:01,300
He rejected me before I could
even finish speaking.

407
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:02,960
You know his temper.

408
00:27:03,550 --> 00:27:05,480
You'd better think of another way.

409
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:06,830
Okay, Mr. Tao.

410
00:27:07,350 --> 00:27:09,410
Sorry for the trouble. I understand.

411
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:10,640
Okay.

412
00:27:15,590 --> 00:27:18,190
How am I supposed to explain
this to Lin Zhixia?

413
00:27:20,110 --> 00:27:21,000
Lin Zhixia?

414
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:22,500
What about her?

415
00:27:24,830 --> 00:27:26,640
She asked me to help her with something.

416
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:30,170
She'd like Professor Liu to write her
a recommendation letter.

417
00:27:31,270 --> 00:27:32,350
But you have no idea.

418
00:27:32,350 --> 00:27:34,210
This old man is really difficult.

419
00:27:34,550 --> 00:27:37,810
Getting a meeting with him
is harder than reaching the sky.

420
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:41,240
The Professor Liu you mentioned,

421
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:42,640
what's his name?

422
00:27:43,550 --> 00:27:44,400
Liu Qingsong.

423
00:27:46,830 --> 00:27:47,590
I see.

424
00:27:48,070 --> 00:27:49,590
Send me Lin Zhixia's materials.

425
00:27:49,590 --> 00:27:50,450
I'll handle it.

426
00:27:52,310 --> 00:27:53,830
Do you know Professor Liu?

427
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,310
If you're talking about the little old man

428
00:27:56,310 --> 00:27:57,720
from your school,

429
00:27:58,270 --> 00:27:59,070
I do know him.

430
00:28:02,550 --> 00:28:04,720
He's the most difficult client
I've ever met.

431
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:06,640
I have a speaker here
that I modified for him.

432
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:09,100
I happen to be delivering it
to him tomorrow.

433
00:28:11,030 --> 00:28:12,430
Wow, what a coincidence.

434
00:28:14,880 --> 00:28:16,160
It's a small world.

435
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:17,440
Okay.

436
00:28:17,750 --> 00:28:20,280
I'll send you the materials
right now, Jiang.

437
00:28:21,030 --> 00:28:21,960
You're the best.

438
00:28:34,770 --> 00:28:37,110
[Runting] [Time-Customized Wedding]

439
00:28:39,990 --> 00:28:44,820
[Runting] [Time-Customized Wedding]

440
00:28:44,820 --> 00:28:46,500
[Inspiration] [Banquet Color]

441
00:28:50,670 --> 00:28:52,450
[Chérie Atelier]

442
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:55,220
[About Style]

443
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:02,550
I'm home.

444
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:03,750
You're back.

445
00:29:05,350 --> 00:29:06,480
Have you had dinner?

446
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:10,840
I have something to tell you.

447
00:29:13,310 --> 00:29:14,030
What is it?

448
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:16,200
Have a seat first.

449
00:29:23,680 --> 00:29:24,550
Have I been

450
00:29:26,030 --> 00:29:27,240
in your way lately?

451
00:29:29,310 --> 00:29:30,240
What do you mean?

452
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:33,590
You...

453
00:29:36,940 --> 00:29:38,870
Do you actually have a girlfriend?

454
00:29:38,960 --> 00:29:41,200
Are you getting married?

455
00:29:42,510 --> 00:29:43,400
I saw wedding brochures

456
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:44,790
on your desk.

457
00:29:45,590 --> 00:29:46,200
I'm sorry.

458
00:29:46,200 --> 00:29:47,270
I didn't mean to pry.

459
00:29:47,270 --> 00:29:49,000
I just... happened to see them.

460
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:53,330
You saw them all?

461
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,350
Why didn't you tell me

462
00:30:01,350 --> 00:30:02,680
that you were getting married?

463
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:04,240
What if she misunderstands?

464
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:04,880
Don't worry.

465
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:06,740
I'll pack up and move out tonight.

466
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:09,310
Sorry for bothering you

467
00:30:09,480 --> 00:30:10,310
all this time.

468
00:30:14,720 --> 00:30:16,580
Is this what you wanted to tell me?

469
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:24,220
Actually, it's my fault.

470
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:26,900
I originally wanted to

471
00:30:27,310 --> 00:30:29,510
tell you after everything was settled.

472
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:33,400
Let me start over.

473
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:34,830
Jin Baihui,

474
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:39,490
I want to be your boyfriend.

475
00:30:44,550 --> 00:30:46,350
The kind that leads to marriage.

476
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:53,240
Wait a minute.

477
00:31:03,750 --> 00:31:05,280
Besides wedding planning,

478
00:31:05,310 --> 00:31:06,640
I've looked at wedding dresses

479
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:07,750
and houses.

480
00:31:08,070 --> 00:31:09,400
Let me tell you about it.

481
00:31:09,590 --> 00:31:10,480
Because I didn't have much time,

482
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:11,940
I only found a few options.

483
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:13,440
But my savings

484
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,900
are enough to pay
the down payment for these.

485
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:17,930
Let me tell you from the beginning.

486
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:18,960
The first one...

487
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,120
It faces south and is well-ventilated.

488
00:31:22,590 --> 00:31:24,050
And then there's this one.

489
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:26,310
The layout isn't as good,

490
00:31:26,310 --> 00:31:27,720
but the lighting is better,

491
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,320
and it has a bright bathroom.

492
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:30,310
And this one.

493
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,550
The lighting isn't as good,

494
00:31:32,550 --> 00:31:34,020
but the community facilities are better.

495
00:31:34,020 --> 00:31:35,350
Which one do you prefer?

496
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:39,630
The layout isn't important.

497
00:31:39,750 --> 00:31:41,480
Are they in a good school district?

498
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:43,070
We need to think about
schooling in the future.

499
00:31:43,070 --> 00:31:45,270
School district... I'm looking for it.

500
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:46,790
This one.

501
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:48,680
This one.

502
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:51,350
This one is assigned
to the City Primary School

503
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:52,640
and City No. 1 High School.

504
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:53,660
And this one.

505
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,000
There are no schools nearby,

506
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,400
but there's a private kindergarten

507
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,720
in the community.

508
00:31:58,270 --> 00:32:00,030
And this one. It's my favorite.

509
00:32:00,110 --> 00:32:03,070
It offers direct promotion from
kindergarten to high school.

510
00:32:03,070 --> 00:32:04,750
Which one do you think is better?

511
00:32:04,750 --> 00:32:06,150
What about medical care?

512
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:08,720
Medical care
is the most important facility

513
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:09,920
for when we retire.

514
00:32:10,110 --> 00:32:11,880
I have options for medical care too.

515
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:12,510
This one.

516
00:32:13,350 --> 00:32:14,880
This one is a 15-minute walk

517
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:16,760
from a top-tier hospital.

518
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:18,110
This one has no hospital nearby,

519
00:32:18,110 --> 00:32:19,640
but it's in a transportation hub.

520
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,480
A 20-minute taxi ride will get us there.

521
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:22,830
I've seen all these houses.

522
00:32:22,830 --> 00:32:23,640
They're pretty good.

523
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:24,400
Pick one.

524
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,400
Pick one you like.

525
00:32:26,030 --> 00:32:27,760
Actually, besides the houses,

526
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:29,270
I also...

527
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:31,440
I also...

528
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:38,490
♪ Only for this lingering warmth
of the moment ♪

529
00:32:34,270 --> 00:32:35,640
Prepared a ring.

530
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:40,640
I know...

531
00:32:39,980 --> 00:32:45,730
♪ Trading souls with the night ♪

532
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:43,680
The girl should choose the ring.

533
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,790
But I wasn't going to tell you,

534
00:32:46,790 --> 00:32:52,570
♪ Every dusk I have stolen ♪

535
00:32:47,510 --> 00:32:49,170
so I made the decision myself.

536
00:32:49,790 --> 00:32:50,790
I picked one

537
00:32:52,270 --> 00:32:53,600
that I think you'd like.

538
00:32:53,810 --> 00:32:59,700
♪ Foretells a parting ♪

539
00:33:01,970 --> 00:33:08,180
♪ Where did the storm start brewing ♪

540
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:07,890
If you don't like it, it's fine.

541
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:08,790
We can exchange it.

542
00:33:08,690 --> 00:33:14,300
♪ Drenching you before we knew it? ♪

543
00:33:09,480 --> 00:33:10,920
We can go buy one you like.

544
00:33:11,310 --> 00:33:12,640
I'm fine with anything.

545
00:33:15,090 --> 00:33:18,020
♪ Let me draw near to you ♪

546
00:33:18,740 --> 00:33:21,690
♪ Let me imagine you ♪

547
00:33:22,180 --> 00:33:24,400
♪ Let me sink into your ♪

548
00:33:24,840 --> 00:33:28,460
♪ Scattered golden glow ♪

549
00:33:29,230 --> 00:33:31,570
♪ Let the night blur your figure ♪

550
00:33:32,540 --> 00:33:35,480
♪ Yet tear myself away from you ♪

551
00:33:36,060 --> 00:33:38,720
♪ I can't fathom why ♪

552
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:42,370
♪ I've never truly possessed you ♪

553
00:33:43,470 --> 00:33:46,810
♪ That blazing, radiant feeling ♪

554
00:33:47,120 --> 00:33:49,940
♪ Once the rain stops, clouds disperse ♪

555
00:33:50,550 --> 00:33:56,550
♪ Hence, time and again, I lose ♪

556
00:33:56,980 --> 00:33:59,800
♪ Myself ♪

557
00:34:26,070 --> 00:34:26,870
What's wrong?

558
00:34:27,480 --> 00:34:28,409
Are you unhappy?

559
00:34:30,550 --> 00:34:31,440
Nothing.

560
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,810
If you don't want to talk to me,

561
00:34:38,550 --> 00:34:40,679
then I won't talk about Professor Liu.

562
00:34:43,110 --> 00:34:44,110
Professor Liu?

563
00:34:46,310 --> 00:34:47,710
Professor Liu Qingsong?

564
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:48,550
Yes.

565
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:49,980
I've already made an appointment with him.

566
00:34:49,980 --> 00:34:51,280
At 9 a.m. tomorrow,

567
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,550
he will come visit you.

568
00:34:52,710 --> 00:34:54,630
But since you don't want to talk to me...

569
00:34:54,630 --> 00:34:55,440
Let's talk.

570
00:34:55,460 --> 00:34:56,060
You...

571
00:34:56,710 --> 00:34:58,070
How did you get an appointment with him?

572
00:34:58,070 --> 00:34:58,880
Duan Qiyan said

573
00:34:58,880 --> 00:35:00,480
he's very hard to talk to.

574
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:02,710
He will definitely come.

575
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:03,510
Tomorrow,

576
00:35:03,630 --> 00:35:05,620
he'll visit your lab.

577
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:07,760
Get the materials ready in advance

578
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:09,690
and just explain it to him clearly.

579
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:11,480
I've communicated with him a few times.

580
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:12,280
I told him

581
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:14,320
a friend of mine
has a very interesting project

582
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:15,450
worth listening to.

583
00:35:15,890 --> 00:35:17,290
You actually know him?

584
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,550
And you can communicate with him anytime?

585
00:35:18,550 --> 00:35:19,800
You are amazing.

586
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:23,930
What else don't I know
about you?

587
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:26,840
It just means you don't know me
well enough.

588
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:28,190
Dr. Lin,

589
00:35:28,190 --> 00:35:29,630
you have a tough battle tomorrow.

590
00:35:29,630 --> 00:35:32,150
First of all, you
need to eat and sleep well.

591
00:35:32,630 --> 00:35:34,110
Do you want some stir-fried beef?

592
00:35:34,110 --> 00:35:34,630
Yes.

593
00:35:34,630 --> 00:35:35,160
Let's go.

594
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:38,280
Tell me again what exactly happened.

595
00:35:38,530 --> 00:35:42,060
[Hematology Department Ward]

596
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:59,090
What are you looking at?

597
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,000
You were so absorbed.

598
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:06,660
Are you nervous about
the experimental treatment?

599
00:36:07,510 --> 00:36:09,310
It's normal for me to be nervous.

600
00:36:11,400 --> 00:36:12,320
But you,

601
00:36:13,590 --> 00:36:14,400
Dr. Shen,

602
00:36:15,150 --> 00:36:16,800
you seem to be

603
00:36:17,110 --> 00:36:18,710
in a really good mood lately.

604
00:36:20,190 --> 00:36:21,000
Really?

605
00:36:25,590 --> 00:36:27,590
It's probably because a patient recently

606
00:36:27,590 --> 00:36:29,760
has been very cooperative
with the treatment.

607
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,630
She followed every piece
of medical advice meticulously.

608
00:36:32,630 --> 00:36:34,160
It saved me a lot of worries.

609
00:36:34,230 --> 00:36:35,670
Don't make it about me.

610
00:36:36,230 --> 00:36:38,290
It's definitely not because of that.

611
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:40,380
Then it must be because...

612
00:36:45,590 --> 00:36:47,190
Look at the weather outside.

613
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:49,130
It's going to rain soon.

614
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:51,800
On rainy days,

615
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,420
we can finally get a good rest.

616
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:10,360
How did you get to know Professor Liu?

617
00:37:12,760 --> 00:37:13,760
You know what,

618
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:17,920
-the canteen's stir-fried beef was great.
-Forget about the stir-fried beef.

619
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:19,780
I'm talking about Professor Liu.

620
00:37:20,400 --> 00:37:21,510
Professor Liu?

621
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:23,950
It's raining.

622
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:26,490
Let's take shelter.

623
00:37:33,550 --> 00:37:34,950
It's raining so heavily.

624
00:37:38,510 --> 00:37:39,440
Wait for me here.

625
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:41,090
I'll go back to the lab
to get an umbrella.

626
00:37:41,090 --> 00:37:41,880
I'll be quick.

627
00:37:41,880 --> 00:37:42,510
No need.

628
00:37:44,230 --> 00:37:45,290
In such heavy rain,

629
00:37:45,730 --> 00:37:48,060
we'll still get wet
even with an umbrella.

630
00:37:48,190 --> 00:37:49,590
We might as well run back.

631
00:37:50,550 --> 00:37:51,530
Let's go, Jiang Yubai!

632
00:37:51,530 --> 00:37:52,390
Lin Zhixia!

633
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:38,480
Go change into dry clothes quickly

634
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:39,740
or you'll catch a cold.

635
00:38:40,030 --> 00:38:40,890
What about you?

636
00:38:41,070 --> 00:38:41,840
I'm fine.

637
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:43,290
Go change your clothes.

638
00:39:57,230 --> 00:39:59,510
Let me dry your hair for you.

639
00:41:31,550 --> 00:41:32,710
I... Um, I...

640
00:41:35,030 --> 00:41:36,030
The rain stopped.

641
00:41:36,190 --> 00:41:37,520
I... I'll get going now.

642
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:51,390
[Nano Eraser]

643
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:51,360
I only realized it later.

644
00:41:52,360 --> 00:41:53,880
Every clumsy approach

645
00:41:54,650 --> 00:41:56,980
and every seemingly unintentional touch

646
00:41:57,510 --> 00:41:59,970
were romantic theorems hidden in formulas,

647
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:02,590
waiting for the final proof.

648
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:05,120
It seemed that

649
00:42:05,860 --> 00:42:07,820
before we even confessed our love,

650
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:11,130
we had already rehearsed the feeling

651
00:42:11,130 --> 00:42:12,500
of being in love a thousand times.
